5. PUT Request:
A. A PUT request is used to update an existing user.
B. The user ID is passed as part of the URL.
C. It requires a request payload with updated user information.
D. The response returns the updated user details along with the update timestamp.
E. The expected HTTP status code is 200 (OK).

6. DELETE Request:
A. A DELETE request is used to remove an existing user.
B. The user ID is passed as part of the URL.
C. No request payload is required.
D. The expected HTTP status code is 204 (No Content).

| Request | Purpose        | Status Code        |
| ------- | -------------- | ------------------ |
| GET     | Retrieve users | **200 OK**         |
| POST    | Create user    | **201 Created**    |
| PUT     | Update user    | **200 OK**         |
| DELETE  | Delete user    | **204 No Content** |
